MTS patch: adults learn other families' languages by living together in
peace (setting mtsLangFullSeconds, 0 or absent = off = stock).

Every mtsLangTickSeconds game seconds (default 6), each pair of living
players of different lineages within mtsLangRadius tiles (default 16, the
speech radius) both learn a fraction of the unlearned weight of the
language between their lineages, at any age. It reuses the stock
first-hearing step (factored out of mapLanguagePhrase as
learnWeightFraction), so the scrambling shrinks word cluster by word
cluster, as it does for children. That step learns at least one whole
cluster per set, so the pace is set by how often it runs: about 50 steps of
1.2% in mtsLangFullSeconds (per tick: chance min(1, r), fraction
1.2% * max(1, r)^2, r = 50 * tick / mtsLangFullSeconds) leave about 5% of
the (frequency-weighted) language unlearned. No learning for a pair
while either is in a kill state (killer or target), either has exiled the
other, or their lineages are at war. The learning maps (stock ones too) are
written to mtsLanguageLearning.txt in the run dir after every tick and
loaded at the first tick, for players alive then (so player saves keep
them; deploy/start.sh deletes the file with the world). mtsLangLog=1 logs
each pair's learned fractions every tick.

